# Reduce motion (System Settings ▸ Accessibility ▸ Display, here cra://debug?reduceMotion=1): ⌘S doesn't slide the
# sidebar and page across the window, the window dissolves from one layout to the other, as Arc 1.174.3's views that
# respectReduceMotion do. With it off the slide plays frame by frame as before (sidebar-slide-live's).
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
pace 0.5
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=reduce
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?reduceMotion=1
expect-log reduce motion: on$
cra://action/toggleSidebar
expect-log sidebar slide: dissolved in [0-9]+ ms \(reduce motion\)
expect-log sidebar slide: page moved [0-9]+ pt over [01] frames
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 0.5
reject-log sidebar slide: page moved [0-9]+ pt over ([2-9]|[1-9][0-9]+) frames
# Off again: Arc's slide, many frames.
cra://debug?reduceMotion=0
expect-log reduce motion: off$
cra://action/toggleSidebar
expect-log sidebar slide: page moved [0-9]+ pt over ([2-9]|[1-9][0-9]+) frames
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 0.5
cra://debug?reduceMotion=system
